      "problem": "$\\sqrt[3]{{9}^{4}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can be written using a fractional exponent as ${x}^{1/n}.$\n\nComparing $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ with $\\sqrt[3]{{9}^{4}},$ we get $x={9}^{4}$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{{9}^{4}}={({9}^{4})}^{1/3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the power law for exponents, we have\n\n$$\n{({9}^{4})}^{1/3}={9}^{4/3}.\n$$",
